humbnail - hiring writer 2026.png","defaultAlt":"featured image","updatedAt":1776114425722,"originalWidth":2400,"originalHeight":1260,"cloudflareId":"014e8530-1d3d-409d-136d-467639157700"},"data-center-construction-di.png":{"id":5243,"filename":"data-center-construction-di.png","defaultAlt":"Line chart of monthly on-site construction spending to build data centers in the United States where spending is relatively flat from 2015 to 2021 and then rises sharply after late 2022 to roughly five-fold higher levels; the series excludes IT hardware like servers and storage. Source: U.S. Census Bureau (2026); U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (2026). License: CC BY.","updatedAt":1787670105340,"originalWidth":1620,"originalHeight":1620,"cloudflareId":"fac09369-5a17-4aa6-58e7-e74992338e00"},"drowning-children-di.png":{"id":5210,"filename":"drowning-children-di.png","defaultAlt":"Line chart of estimated global drowning death rates per 100,000 children for ages under 5 and ages 5 to 14 from 1980 to 2023, where both lines decline steadily and the under-5 rate remains consistently higher than the 5 to 14 rate. Source: IHME, Global Burden of Disease (2025). License: CC BY. Note: estimates include unintentional drownings (ponds, wells, bathtubs) and exclude drownings in floods, boat accidents, suicides, and homicides.","updatedAt":1787146567053,"originalWidth":1620,"originalHeight":1620,"cloudflareId":"10126e3d-64fb-4481-d289-c005f7f99000"},"guyana-gdp-growth.png":{"id":5189,"filename":"guyana-gdp-growth.png","defaultAlt":"Line chart of GDP per capita for selected countries from 1990 to 2026 (international-$ at 2021 prices, adjusted for inflation and differences in living costs) where Guyana's line shows a sharp increase after oil production began in December 2019, indicating the fastest recent GDP per capita growth among the countries shown. Data source: Eurostat, OECD, IMF, and World Bank (2026). License: CC BY.","updatedAt":1786525095403,"originalWidth":1620,"originalHeight":1620,"cloudflareId":"656bec92-4a07-43f8-befc-6521aae9b600"},"meat-preferences-by-country.png":{"id":5191,"filename":"meat-preferences-by-country.png","defaultAlt":"Stacked bar chart of meat supply breakdown by type across countries where the visualization shows wide variation in dominant meats — for example, Brazil and Argentina have large poultry and beef shares, Germany and China have large pork shares, and India and Japan have high fish and seafood shares. Data are for 2023 except Japan (2022); source: Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (2025). License: CC BY.","updatedAt":1786530136716,"originalWidth":1620,"originalHeight":1620,"cloudflareId":"af3f7962-1cb1-4558-7034-7cc6504a5100"},"new-cases-malaria-per-100.png":{"id":5190,"filename":"new-cases-malaria-per-100.png","defaultAlt":"Horizontal arrow chart of new malaria cases per 100 people in selected high-burden countries where it compares values in 2000 and 2023 to show declines over time. The chart shows cases falling from about 41 to 49 in 2000 down to roughly 28 to 36 in 2023, with most worst-affected countries still around 30 cases per 100 people. Source: IHME, Global Burden of Disease (2025). License: CC BY.","updatedAt":1786527212951,"originalWidth":1620,"originalHeight":1620,"cloudflareId":"6ec31df4-09e8-41f4-bedc-847c3bdeb400"},"oda-share-gni-ranking-2025.png":{"id":5168,"filename":"oda-share-gni-ranking-2025.png","defaultAlt":"Horizontal bar chart of official development assistance (ODA) as a share of gross national income for selected developed countries in 2025, where it shows four countries (Norway, Luxembourg, Sweden, and Denmark) meeting the UN target of 0.7 percent of national income, while most others fall below that level. Source: OECD (2026). License: CC BY.","updatedAt":1786013468751,"originalWidth":1620,"originalHeight":1620,"cloudflareId":"1d41ad85-1bae-49ff-b3bd-d2a8da39df00"},"thailand-peak-population.png":{"id":5169,"filename":"thailand-peak-population.png","defaultAlt":"Li