]},{"id":1826,"path":[1837,1510,1826],"name":"Military Personnel & Spending","slug":"military-personnel-spending","isTopic":1,"isSearchable":1,"weight":103,"children":[]},{"id":289,"path":[1837,1510,289],"name":"Violence Against Children & Children's Rights","slug":"violence-against-rights-for-children","isTopic":1,"isSearchable":1,"weight":102,"children":[]}]}]},"announcements":[{"id":"1qH-WkK3hDKxSKFURagpFsqRuJyxbVg9fw_ajxhfdUBc","title":"New data: World Development Indicators, July 2026 release","slug":"new-data-world-development-indicators-july-2026-release","authors":["Mojmír Vinkler"],"publishedAt":"August 31, 2026","published":true,"excerpt":"Explore updated data on global development from the World Bank.","type":"announcement","kicker":"data-update"},{"id":"1YuZg9mKwM0NDh0lxhJHpHeBh3OAX_AlTjChIK2b9J2I","title":"How does the World Bank classify countries by income?","slug":"how-does-the-world-bank-classify-countries-by-income","authors":["Pablo Arriagada"],"publishedAt":"August 24, 2026","published":true,"excerpt":"Explore updated data on income groups from the World Bank.","type":"announcement","kicker":"data-update"},{"id":"1vI2sPYWYagpekwJZPsrSE_T7oOlrOwgF0N_d2NxtUZA","title":"The number of whales killed globally peaked in the 1960s","slug":"the-number-of-whales-killed-globally-peaked-in-the-1960s","authors":["Tuna Acisu"],"publishedAt":"August 17, 2026","published":true,"excerpt":"Explore updated data from the International Whaling Commission.","type":"announcement","kicker":"data-update"}]},"latestDataInsights":[{"id":"1oZJlx0vJBbqAr2o0H21hvzAzt0F-P3jzMB5kMvYzHVw","slug":"money-spent-on-building-data-centers-in-the-us-has-grown-5-fold-since-late-2022","publishedAt":"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"narrow","type":"image","filename":"data-center-construction-di.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"The United States is home to ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.datacentermap.com/usa/","children":[{"text":"thousands of data centers","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":". They are part of the infrastructure that powers many digital services, including email, gaming, streaming, social media, and, increasingly, artificial intelligence (AI).","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"As this chart shows, between 2018 and 2022, spending on building data centers in the US hovered between $500 million and $1 billion per month (when adjusted for inflation).","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"But since late 2022, large investments in AI have led to a rapid growth in data center construction — both by expanding existing facilities and building new, larger ones.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"The latest figures released by the US Census Bureau estimate that $4.4 billion was spent in June 2026 alone — a 5-fold increase compared to November 2022, when ChatGPT was released by OpenAI.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"These figures cover privately-funded construction and represent only the money spent on building the actual facilities, including materials and construction labor. They don’t include the cost of IT hardware like servers and storage, which can represent a very large share of total investment.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/artificial-intelligence#all-charts","text":"Explore our interactive charts on artificial intelligence","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"Money spent on building data centers in the US has grown 5-fold since late 2022","authors":["Edouard Mathieu"],"figma-url":"","authorRoles":{},"grapher-url":"","narrative-chart":"data-center-construction-di"}},{"id":"1KcaDlxlweWrDKQ_ghDPrT4Q5qgdXcsBx4CmJeH1YSqI","slug":"how-often-are-people-infected-with-malaria","publishedAt":"2026-08-29T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"narrow","type":"image","filename":"new-cases-malaria-per-100.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Malaria is an infectious disease that kills over ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/malaria-deaths-by-region","children":[{"text":"600,000 people","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":" a year. Most of them, children.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Its high death toll is at least partly explained by the fact that there are so many infections every year: an estimated ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/estimated-number-of-malaria-cases","children":[{"text":"260 to 310 million","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"I was curious to know how often people living in the worst-affected areas are infected with malaria. In the chart, you can see estimates of new cases per 100 people across high-burden countries. In recent decades, infection rates have declined but remain very high. There are around 30 new cases per 100 people each year.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"It would be tempting to simplify this number and say that 30% of people living in Nigeria are infected each year. But that’s probably far from reality.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"This is because the same people are often reinfected. When I looked at the scientific literature, I was surprised by how often. A ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.ajtmh.org/view/journals/tpmd/103/2/article-p785.xml","children":[{"text":"study","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":" focused on children in Uganda found that those without preventative measures were infected around five times per year. Another found that in Burkina Faso, it was ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0050036","children":[{"text":"up to six times","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"So, the reality behind the “30 cases per 100 people” average is probably very skewed. Many — particularly children who have not built up immunity — are infected multiple times per year, while most of the population is not infected at all.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/malaria","text":"Explore more data on the global burden of malaria","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"How often are people infected with malaria?","authors":["Hannah Ritchie"],"figma-url":"https://www.figma.com/design/s6Sv60bakebRRW2TxsMQbF/Charts--2026-?node-id=24852-12&t=m3EWYJMZhRFkDT9A-0","authorRoles":{},"grapher-url":"","narrative-chart":""}},{"id":"168VrLCQAlJq3gllZT1CGDS3slzX-LWeSQayHDyWJFH0","slug":"drowning-is-a-common-cause-of-death-among-children-the-world-has-made-progress-but-more-can-be-done","publishedAt":"2026-08-27T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"narrow","type":"image","filename":"drowning-children-di.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"More than 100,000 children under the age of 15 died from drowning in 2023. I found this statistic staggering when I first saw it. Drowning is one of the ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/causes-of-death-in-5-14-year-olds","children":[{"text":"top causes of death","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":" among older children.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"The World Health Organization ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/drowning","children":[{"text":"explains","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":" that around 90% of all drowning deaths occur in low- and middle-income countries. There, much of the risk comes from everyday exposure to water in ponds, rivers, and lakes used for bathing and washing clothes, or open wells ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/what-no-safe-water-means","children":[{"text":"used to collect water","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Deaths like these can be prevented, and they increasingly are. Drowning used to be far more common than it is today. That’s the focus of the chart.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"In 1980, almost 30 children under five died from drowning for every 100,000 children in that age group. By 2023, this rate had fallen to 7.4. Death rates among older children also fell substantially.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Targeted measures can reduce drowning risks. These include covering wells, using doorway barriers or playpens to keep young children away from water, and water-safety training, ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789241511933","children":[{"text":"among others","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Rising living standards matter as well, and much of the decline in the chart reflects this. As many countries have become richer, ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-the-population-using-improved-water-sources-wash?tab=slope&country=OWID_LIC~TZA~MOZ~SLE~ETH~SOM","children":[{"text":"access to safe water has improved","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":", so fewer families depend on ponds and open wells for everyday needs.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/what-do-people-die-from-in-different-countries","text":"Drowning is one of many causes of child deaths. Which ones are the most common? We recently built a visualization that lets you explore this for any country, across different age groups.","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"Drowning is a common cause of death among children — the world has made progress, but more can be done","authors":["Esteban Ortiz-Ospina"],"figma-url":"","authorRoles":{},"grapher-url":"","narrative-chart":"https://admin.owid.io/admin/narrative-charts/339/edit?tab=text"}},{"id":"1Xt-BlIJhtSRkOX1nu0h36-kQmtZSJbwboDo9ewykD68","slug":"meat-preferences-vary-a-lot-across-different-countries","publishedAt":"2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"wide","type":"image","filename":"meat-preferences-by-country.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"America’s most popular type of meat is chicken. In Argentina, it’s beef. And in Japan, it’s seafood.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"There are large differences in the popularity of meat types across the world.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"In the chart, you can see the share of supply that comes from different types of meat: poultry, beef, pork, sheep and goat, and fish and seafood. I’ve picked just a selection of countries that highlight some of the variation across the world.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Of course, countries also eat very different ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/per-capita-meat-type","children":[{"text":"amounts","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":" of meat; this chart focuses on the relative quantities in national diets.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"This data comes from the ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/","children":[{"text":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/per-capita-meat-type?stackMode=relative","text":"Explore the most popular types of meat in your country in the global dataset","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"Meat preferences vary a lot across different countries","authors":["Hannah Ritchie","Pablo Arriagada"],"figma-url":"https://www.figma.com/design/s6Sv60bakebRRW2TxsMQbF/Charts--2026-?node-id=24853-5","authorRoles":{},"narrative-chart":"per-capita-meat-and-fish-consumption-di"}},{"id":"1EF1XNnViAjWdoJZbjRjXnjFv-hgdg6Ahp7UjUYXqskM","slug":"thailands-population-may-have-already-peaked","publishedAt":"2026-08-22T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"narrow","type":"image","filename":"thailand-peak-population.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Many countries are in a fairly unique demographic position in history: their populations are shrinking not due to a temporary shock but to sustained structural decline.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"If we look at the United Nations’ population estimates and medium projections, 66 countries and territories ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/population-peak-status","children":[{"text":"had already passed","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":" peak population this year. Almost all of them are in Europe and East Asia.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"But there is one country in Southeast Asia in this position: Thailand. As you can see in the chart, the UN projects that its population will continue to fall throughout this century.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"This is the result of a rapid drop in fertility rates. In 1970, women in Thailand had an average of 6 children; twenty years later, that had fallen to 2. This was as fast as ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/children-born-per-woman?country=THA~CHN","children":[{"text":"China’s decline","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":". Today, the rate is at most 1.2 children per woman, and some national statistics put it closer to 1.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"What makes Thailand unusual is that this happened while it was still a ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.amazon.co.uk/Thailands-Reproductive-Revolution-Fertility-Demography/dp/0299110540","children":[{"text":"relatively poor country","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":". In 1970, it launched its National Family Planning Program. This was voluntary and non-coercive, but effectively increased contraceptive use, family planning access, and education levels for women.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/population-peak-status","text":"Explore which other countries may have already peaked","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"Thailand’s population may have already peaked","authors":["Hannah Ritchie","Edouard Mathieu","Lucas Rodés-Guirao"],"figma-url":"https://www.figma.com/design/s6Sv60bakebRRW2TxsMQbF/Charts--2026-?node-id=24565-12244&t=Knw25q3rqJKTpEKj-0","authorRoles":{},"grapher-url":"","narrative-chart":"thailand-peak-population"}},{"id":"1OqJB6v-dZCIOgg3qAvHbiTxK_uAJHAp2Fa2BIpPo1VE","slug":"four-developed-countries-met-the-uns-target-for-foreign-aid-in2025","publishedAt":"2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"narrow","type":"image","filename":"oda-share-gni-ranking-2025.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"In the 1970s, the UN General Assembly adopted a resolution asking developed countries to contribute at least 0.7% of their national income to foreign aid. Most countries ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://web-archive.oecd.org/temp/2024-06-17/63452-the07odagnitarget-ahistory.htm","children":[{"text":"signed off on this goal","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":", except for Switzerland and the United States.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"But very few countries have met this target in the fifty years since then. Even today, only a handful of countries do.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"In 2023, five countries ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/data-insights/five-developed-countries-met-the-uns-target-for-foreign-aid-in2023","children":[{"text":"met this target","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":": Norway, Luxembourg, Sweden, Germany, and Denmark. Two years on, this has dropped to four, as Germany’s contribution shrank to 0.6%.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"As you can see in the chart, other developed countries give less than 0.7% of their national income.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/foreign-aid","text":"Explore more of our charts on foreign aid: who contributes, and where it goes","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"Four developed countries met the UN’s target for foreign aid in 2025","authors":["Hannah Ritchie","Pablo Arriagada"],"figma-url":"https://www.figma.com/design/s6Sv60bakebRRW2TxsMQbF/Charts--2026-?node-id=24359-2","authorRoles":{},"grapher-url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/foreign-aid-given-as-a-share-of-national-income-net?tab=map"}},{"id":"1LXMpaUK7oPdZwWWdJn1iJb3yur8bXFGQKOqNjrcn2-4","slug":"guyanas-oil-driven-economy-has-had-the-largest-gdp-per-capita-growth-in-the-world-in-recent-years","publishedAt":"2026-08-18T00:00:00.000Z","content":{"body":[{"size":"narrow","type":"image","filename":"guyana-gdp-growth.png","hasOutline":true,"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Guyana, a small country in South America, has seen the fastest growth in gross domestic product (","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"id":"gdp","children":[{"text":"GDP","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-dod"},{"text":") per capita in the world over the past decade.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"This is illustrated in the chart, which shows GDP per capita for Guyana and several other countries, based on estimates from the World Bank.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"The data is adjusted for inflation, so Guyana’s sharp growth is not due to price changes over time.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"A large and sudden expansion in oil production has driven most of this growth. Between 2020 and 2025, the country’s ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/fossil-fuels?tab=line&country=%7EGUY&fuel=oil&metric=production&per_capita=total","children":[{"text":"oil production grew 860%","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":", making it a ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=62103","children":[{"text":"key contributor to global crude oil supply growth","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"Before oil extraction started, Guyana’s GDP per capita was well below the global average. It is now more than three times higher.","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"type":"text","value":[{"text":"It’s too early to see the full effects of this, and hard to measure how far the oil boom has translated into better living standards in the country. Official poverty estimates, for example, have not been published since production began. But there is early evidence of the government channeling oil revenue toward citizens, for instance, through ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/06/guyana-cash-payouts-oil-wealth","children":[{"text":"cash grants for every adult","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":", ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/7/irfaan-ali-reelected-for-second-term-as-oil-rich-guyanas-president","children":[{"text":"free tuition at public universities","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":", and ","spanType":"span-simple-text"},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/annual-healthcare-expenditure-per-capita?tab=line&country=~GUY","children":[{"text":"increasing health spending","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"spanType":"span-link"},{"text":".","spanType":"span-simple-text"}],"parseErrors":[]},{"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/fossil-fuels","text":"Read more about oil production and fossil fuels","type":"cta","parseErrors":[]}],"refs":{"errors":[],"definitions":{}},"type":"data-insight","title":"Guyana’s oil-driven economy has seen the world’s fastest growth in GDP per capita in recent years","authors":["Esteban Ortiz-Ospina","Pablo Arriagada"],"figma-url":"https://www.figma.com/design/s6Sv60bakebRRW2TxsMQbF/Charts--2026-?node-id=24363-2","approved-by":"Hannah","authorRoles":{},"narrative-chart":"gdp-per-capita-guyana"}}]}</script><script>
function setJSEnabled(enabled) {
    var elem = window.document.documentElement;
    if (enabled) {
        elem.classList.remove("js-disabled");
        elem.classList.add("js-enabled");
    } else {
        elem.classList.remove("js-enabled");
